Clients must have a USFSA/USA Hockey registration number to sign up. This number is given to them from the USFSA/USA Hockey organization. USA Hockey numbers change each season; US Figure Skating members seem to keep theirs. *Since 2026-10-16: US Figure Skating, USA Hockey or Learn to Skate USA (ADR-029); other organizations, Kim §12.*
    Check to see if there is an API to check if the number is valid for the year/season.  *No way to verify it is valid as of now. Coach can verify themselves if they care*
    *Design:* the number is per skater, not per account. Each skater picks U.S. Figure Skating (member number),
    USA Hockey (registration number) or Learn to Skate USA (member number; added to the design 2026-10-20) and enters the number. The hint says USA Hockey numbers change every season.
    *Decided 2026-10-12:* required for every skater. Phase 1 takes USFSA or USA Hockey only; Skate Canada and Hockey Canada are Phase 2.
    *Decided 2026-10-16:* Learn to Skate USA numbers are accepted too, for beginners. Everyone must have a number (Kim). (ADR-029)
    *Validation:* the number is a free-text box, so it must be checked and cleaned up before it's saved:
        trim spaces, uppercase, check it against a pattern for its organization (allowed characters only), cap the length,
        and store the cleaned-up form. This checks the shape only, not that the number is real.
        USA Hockey: 14 characters, 9 digits and 5 letters, with a check digit that changes each season (a setting, not code).
        US Figure Skating: format not yet known; get it from a real card or Kim. See ADR-029 and Open-Pending §2b.
        Learn to Skate USA: format not yet known either; ~~digits only within a loose length range until known~~ letters
          and digits, 1 to 20 characters, like U.S. Figure Skating (owner, 2026-11-06; Kim §9 Q7 still open).
    *Decided by the owner 2026-11-06, settling a conflict with the Harbor design (screens-account.js, acNumError):*
        US Figure Skating and Learn to Skate USA numbers are letters and digits, 1 to 20 characters. Anything else is
        refused with "Use letters and numbers only." or "That's too long for a member number."
        A rejected number gets a message naming the expected shape (for USA Hockey, "14 characters, 9 digits and
        5 letters"), never a hint that the number was looked up.
        *(from ADR-029, amendment 2026-11-06 and decision 4, moved 2026-11-08)*
        *Ruled by the owner 2026-11-09.* The designs already use this rule.

